# n 'f n_wise v reduces f over every window of n consecutive major
# cells (B21, APL2's N f/ V): 2 '- the differences, 3 '+ moving sums,
# 2 'c_at the pairs; a negative n reverses each window; n of the length
# is one window, one more is none, 0 gives the identity once more than
# there are items; a matrix goes by rows, a subscript along that axis.
== SOURCE
2 '- n_wise 1 4 9 16
-2 '- n_wise 1 4 9 16
3 '+ n_wise 1 2 3 4 5
2 'c_at n_wise "abcd"
4 '+ n_wise 1 2 3 4
t_ally 5 '+ n_wise 1 2 3 4
0 '+ n_wise 1 2 3
2 '+ n_wise 3 2 r_eshape r_ange 6
2 '- n_wise_2 2 3 r_eshape 1 4 9 2 3 5
== RESULT
-3 -5 -7
3 5 7
6 9 12
ab
bc
cd
10
0
0 0 0 0
4  6
8 10
-3 -5
-1 -2
